('00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000031', 'semio-l4-vocab', 'semio', 4, 'choice', 'intermediate', 'Sémiologie Médicale', 'Pathologie', '{"kind":"choice","prompt":"Select the clinical consequence connector: ''Essential hypertension remains asymptomatic for years; _______, it is frequently referred to as the silent killer.''","options":["therefore","whereas","although","in order to"],"correctAnswer":"therefore"}', 'Select the clinical consequence connector: ''Essential hypertension remains asymptomatic for years; _______, it is frequently referred to as the silent killer.''', 'Sélectionnez le connecteur de conséquence clinique : ''Essential hypertension remains asymptomatic for years; _______, it is frequently referred to as the silent killer.''', 'اختر رابط النتيجة السريرية : ''Essential hypertension remains asymptomatic for years; _______, it is frequently referred to as the silent killer.''', NULL, 'therefore', 25, '', '', '', 0.5, 0.5),
('00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000032', 'physio-l4-vocab', 'physio', 4, 'wordbank', 'advanced', 'Physiologie', 'Neurologie', '{"kind":"wordbank","prompt":"Arrange this temporal and sequential physiological sentence:","tokens":["When","action","potentials","reach","axon","terminals","neurotransmitters","are","released","into","synapses"],"correctAnswer":"When action potentials reach axon terminals neurotransmitters are released into synapses"}', 'Arrange this temporal and sequential physiological sentence:', 'Remettez en ordre cette phrase temporelle décrivant la transmission synaptique :', 'رتب هذه الجملة الزمنية التي تصف مراحل النقل المشبكي :', NULL, 'When action potentials reach axon terminals neurotransmitters are released into synapses', 25, '', '', '', 0.5, 0.5),
('00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000033', 'anat-l5-vocab', 'anat', 5, 'choice', 'advanced', 'Anatomie', 'Ostéologie', '{"kind":"choice","prompt":"According to the medical text passage, what cellular imbalance primarily leads to the development of osteoporosis?","options":["Osteoclasts resorb bone faster than osteoblasts can synthesize it","Osteoblasts hypersecrete mineralized matrix","Bone marrow ceases red blood cell production","Synovial fluid is absorbed into the periosteum"],"correctAnswer":"Osteoclasts resorb bone faster than osteoblasts can synthesize it"}', 'According to the medical text passage, what cellular imbalance primarily leads to the development of osteoporosis?', 'D''après l''extrait médical, quel déséquilibre cellulaire conduit principalement au développement de l''ostéoporose ?', 'وفقاً للنص الطبي، ما هو الخلل الخلوي الرئيسي الذي يؤدي لحدوث هشاشة العظام؟', NULL, 'Osteoclasts resorb bone faster than osteoblasts can synthesize it', 30, 'Bone is a dynamic living tissue undergoing continuous remodeling through the coupled activities of osteoblasts (bone-forming cells) and osteoclasts (bone-resorbing cells). In healthy adults, the rate of bone formation equals bone resorption. However, with aging or hormonal deficiency (such as postmenopausal estrogen decline), osteoclastic activity outpaces osteoblastic synthesis, resulting in osteoporosis characterized by decreased bone mineral density and increased susceptibility to fragility fractures of the femoral neck and vertebrae.', 'L''os est un tissu vivant dynamique subissant un remodelage permanent assuré par les ostéoblastes et les ostéoclastes. Avec l''âge ou la ménopause, l''activité ostéoclastique dépasse la synthèse ostéoblastique, conduisant à l''ostéoporose et aux fractures de fragilité.', 'العظم نسيج حي يخضع لإعادة تشكيل مستمرة بتوازن بين الخلايا البانية والكاسرة للعظم. مع التقدم في العمر أو نقص الإستروجين، يتفوق نشاط الخلايا الكاسرة مما يؤدي لهشاشة العظام والكسور المرضية.', 0.5, 0.5),
('00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000034', 'anat-l5-vocab', 'anat', 5, 'choice', 'advanced', 'Anatomie', 'Arthrologie', '{"kind":"choice","prompt":"How does avascular articular cartilage receive its metabolic nourishment according to the text?","options":["Via direct diffusion from the synovial fluid","Through deep penetrating periosteal blood vessels","Exclusively from the yellow bone marrow","Via the epiphyseal nutrient artery"],"correctAnswer":"Via direct diffusion from the synovial fluid"}', 'How does avascular articular cartilage receive its metabolic nourishment according to the text?', 'Comment le cartilage articulaire avasculaire reçoit-il ses nutriments selon le texte ?', 'كيف يتغذى الغضروف المفصلي الخالي من الأوعية الدموية بحسب ما ورد في النص؟', NULL, 'Via direct diffusion from the synovial fluid', 30, 'Synovial joints, or diarthroses, are engineered to minimize friction and resist mechanical shear during ambulation. The articulating osseous surfaces are capped by avascular, aneural articular cartilage composed mainly of type II collagen and proteoglycans. Surrounding the joint cavity is the fibrous articular capsule, lined internally by the synovial membrane. This membrane secretes synovial fluid, an ultrafiltrate of blood plasma containing hyaluronic acid and lubricin, which lubricates the articular surfaces and nourishes chondrocytes via diffusion.', 'Les diarthroses sont conçues pour minimiser les frottements. Les surfaces sont recouvertes de cartilage articulaire avasculaire nourri par diffusion à partir du liquide synovial sécrété par la membrane synoviale.', 'صُممت المفاصل الزليلية لتقليل الاحتكاك. تغطى أسطح العظام بغضروف مفصلي خالٍ من الأوعية والأعصاب يتغذى عبر الانتشار من السائل الزليلي الذي تفرزه المحفظة الزليلية.', 0.5, 0.5),
('00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000035', 'physio-l5-vocab', 'physio', 5, 'choice', 'advanced', 'Physiologie', 'Myologie & Neurologie', '{"kind":"choice","prompt":"What enzyme terminates the synaptic signaling action of acetylcholine at the motor end plate?","options":["Acetylcholinesterase","ATP synthase","Creatine kinase","Alkaline phosphatase"],"correctAnswer":"Acetylcholinesterase"}', 'What enzyme terminates the synaptic signaling action of acetylcholine at the motor end plate?', 'Quelle enzyme met fin à l''action synaptique de l''acétylcholine au niveau de la plaque motrice ?', 'ما هو الإنزيم المسؤول عن إيقاف الإشارة المشبكية للأسيتيل كولين في الصفيحة الحركية؟', NULL, 'Acetylcholinesterase', 30, 'Transmission of nerve impulses to skeletal muscle occurs at specialized synapses known as neuromuscular junctions (NMJs). When a motor action potential depolarizes the presynaptic terminal, voltage-gated calcium channels open, prompting exocytosis of acetylcholine (ACh) into the synaptic cleft. ACh rapidly binds nicotinic receptors on the folded motor end plate, triggering sodium influx and end-plate potential generation. Acetylcholinesterase rapidly hydrolyzes ACh, terminating the signal to permit subsequent muscle twitch relaxation.', 'La transmission neuromusculaire s''effectue par libération d''acétylcholine (ACh) au niveau de la fente synaptique. L''acétylcholinestérase détruit rapidement l''ACh pour permettre le relâchement musculaire.', 'يتم نقل الإشارة العصبية في الوصلة العصبية العضلية بتحرير الأسيتيل كولين، ويقوم إنزيم أستيل كولين إستيراز بإيقاف الإشارة لتمكين استرخاء الليف العضلي.', 0.5, 0.5),
('00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000036', 'physio-l5-vocab', 'physio', 5, 'choice', 'advanced', 'Physiologie', 'Respiratoire', '{"kind":"choice","prompt":"What critical physiological role does pulmonary surfactant perform according to the text?","options":["Lowers surface tension to prevent alveolar collapse at expiration","Transports oxygen directly into capillary hemoglobin","Phagocytizes inhaled pathogens in the terminal bronchiole","Increases systemic blood pressure during inspiration"],"correctAnswer":"Lowers surface tension to prevent alveolar collapse at expiration"}', 'What critical physiological role does pulmonary surfactant perform according to the text?', 'Quel rôle physiologique fondamental joue le surfactant pulmonaire d''après le texte ?', 'ما هو الدور الفسيولوجي الحيوي الذي يقوم به السطحي الرئوي (Surfactant) بحسب النص؟', NULL, 'Lowers surface tension to prevent alveolar collapse at expiration', 30, 'The human respiratory system accomplishes gas exchange across an ultra-thin blood-air barrier in approximately 400 million alveoli. The alveolar surface consists predominantly of flat type I pneumocytes facilitating passive O2 and CO2 diffusion, alongside cuboidal type II pneumocytes. Type II cells synthesize pulmonary surfactant, a complex lipoprotein containing dipalmitoylphosphatidylcholine. By lowering alveolar surface tension, surfactant prevents end-expiratory atelectasis and equalizes pressure among alveoli of varying diameters.', 'Le système respiratoire assure les échanges gazeux au niveau de 400 millions d''alvéoles. Les pneumocytes de type II synthétisent le surfactant qui abaisse la tension superficielle et évite l''atélectasie expiratoire.', 'تحتوي الرئتان على نحو 400 مليون سنخ رئوي للتبادل الغازي. تفرز خلايا السنخ من النوع الثاني مادة السطحي الرئوي التي تمنع انخماص الأسناخ عند الزفير.', 0.5, 0.5),
('00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000037', 'physio-l5-vocab', 'physio', 5, 'choice', 'advanced', 'Physiologie', 'Cardiovasculaire', '{"kind":"choice","prompt":"Which cranial nerve provides the primary parasympathetic resting tone to the sinoatrial pacemaker?","options":["Vagus nerve (CN X)","Trigeminal nerve (CN V)","Facial nerve (CN VII)","Hypoglossal nerve (CN XII)"],"correctAnswer":"Vagus nerve (CN X)"}', 'Which cranial nerve provides the primary parasympathetic resting tone to the sinoatrial pacemaker?', 'Quel nerf crânien assure le tonus vagal parasympathique de repos sur le nœud sinusal ?', 'أي عصب قحفي يوفر النبرة نظيرة الودية الأساسية لتنظيم نبضات العقدة الجيبية الأذينية في وضع الراحة؟', NULL, 'Vagus nerve (CN X)', 30, 'The sinoatrial (SA) node located in the superior wall of the right atrium acts as the physiological cardiac pacemaker, generating spontaneous action potentials at an intrinsic rate of 100 beats per minute. Under resting conditions, tonic parasympathetic stimulation via the vagus nerve (cranial nerve X) releases acetylcholine to slow pacemaker firing down to 60-70 bpm (vagal tone). During physical exertion or stress, sympathetic adrenergic stimulation increases sodium and calcium influx, elevating heart rate and contractile force.', 'Le nœud sinusal génère un rythme spontané de 100 bpm. Au repos, le contingent parasympathique du nerf vague (X) libère de l''acétylcholine pour ralentir la fréquence à 60-70 bpm (tonus vagal).', 'تولد العقدة الجيبية الأذينية إشارات ذاتية بمعدل 100 نبضة/دقيقة، بينما يقوم العصب المبهم (العاشر) بكبحها فسيولوجياً أثناء الراحة إلى 60-70 نبضة/دقيقة.', 0.5, 0.5),
('00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000038', 'anat-l5-vocab', 'anat', 5, 'choice', 'advanced', 'Anatomie', 'Ostéologie & Rachis', '{"kind":"choice","prompt":"What anatomical component provides central gelatinous shock absorption within an intervertebral disc?","options":["Nucleus pulposus","Annulus fibrosus","Ligamentum flavum","Spinous process"],"correctAnswer":"Nucleus pulposus"}', 'What anatomical component provides central gelatinous shock absorption within an intervertebral disc?', 'Quel élément anatomique assure l''amortissement gélatineux au centre du disque intervertébral ?', 'ما هو المكون التشريحي الذي يوفر امتصاص الصدمات الجيلاتيني في مركز القرص بين الفقري؟', NULL, 'Nucleus pulposus', 30, 'The human vertebral column consists of 33 vertebrae during infancy, consolidating into 26 distinct functional bones in adulthood: 7 cervical, 12 thoracic, 5 lumbar, the sacrum (5 fused vertebrae), and the coccyx (4 fused segments). Intervertebral discs situated between adjacent vertebral bodies consist of a tough outer annulus fibrosus and a gelatinous central nucleus pulposus. These discs absorb vertical shocks and grant multi-directional spinal flexibility while safeguarding the enclosed spinal cord.', 'La colonne vertébrale adulte compte 26 os. Les disques intervertébraux comprennent un anneau fibreux périphérique (annulus fibrosus) et un noyau gélatineux central (nucleus pulposus) amortisseur de chocs.', 'يتكون العمود الفقري البالغ من 26 عظمة. تتكون الأقراص بين الفقرية من حلقة ليفية محيطية ونواة لبية جيلاتينية مركزية لامتصاص الصدمات وحماية النخاع الشوكي.', 0.5, 0.5),
('00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000039', 'anapath-l6-vocab', 'anapath', 6, 'choice', 'advanced', 'Anatomie Pathologique', 'Genou', '{"kind":"choice","prompt":"Which knee ligament is most likely completely ruptured in this young athlete?","options":["Anterior cruciate ligament (ACL)","Posterior cruciate ligament (PCL)","Medial collateral ligament (MCL)","Patellar tendon"],"correctAnswer":"Anterior cruciate ligament (ACL)"}', 'Which knee ligament is most likely completely ruptured in this young athlete?', 'Quel ligament du genou est très probablement rompu chez ce jeune footballeur ?', 'أي أربطة الركبة هو الأكثر احتمالاً للتعرض للتمزق الكامل لدى هذا الرياضي؟', NULL, 'Anterior cruciate ligament (ACL)', 35, 'Clinical Vignette: A 21-year-old competitive soccer player is evaluated after an acute injury. While rapidly decelerating and twisting on a firmly planted right foot, he felt an audible ''pop'' inside the knee, followed by intense pain and inability to continue playing. Examination 2 hours later demonstrates marked joint effusion (hemarthrosis). The Lachman test is strongly positive with an absent firm endpoint. Anterior drawer test is positive, whereas posterior drawer and collateral stress tests are normal.', 'Vignette Clinique : Footballeur de 21 ans présentant une entorse grave du genou droit avec bruit de craquement audible en torsion, hémarthrose rapide et test de Lachman nettement positif.', 'حالة سريرية: لاعب كرة قدم يبلغ 21 عاماً أصيب أثناء المباراة بحركة التوائية مفاجئة مع صوت طقطقة وتورم سريع بالركبة، وفحص لاخمان إيجابي دون نقطة توقف صلبة.', 0.5, 0.5),
('00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000040', 'anapath-l6-vocab', 'anapath', 6, 'choice', 'advanced', 'Anatomie Pathologique', 'Membre Supérieur', '{"kind":"choice","prompt":"Which peripheral nerve is chronically compressed in this clinical presentation of Carpal Tunnel Syndrome?","options":["Median nerve","Ulnar nerve","Radial nerve","Musculocutaneous nerve"],"correctAnswer":"Median nerve"}', 'Which peripheral nerve is chronically compressed in this clinical presentation of Carpal Tunnel Syndrome?', 'Quel nerf périphérique est comprimé dans ce syndrome du canal carpien ?', 'أي عصب محيطي يتعرض للانضغاط في متلازمة النفق الرسغي لهذه المريضة؟', NULL, 'Median nerve', 35, 'Clinical Vignette: A 46-year-old office worker presents with a 6-month history of nocturnal burning pain, numbness, and tingling in the palmar surface of the thumb, index, and middle fingers of her right hand. Shaking the hand temporarily relieves the symptoms (flick sign). Physical exam shows mild atrophy of the thenar eminence. Phalen''s test reproduces paresthesia within 30 seconds, and percussion over the volar wrist crease (Tinel''s sign) causes tingling in the same digits.', 'Vignette Clinique : Patiente de 46 ans se plaignant d''engourdissements nocturnes des trois premiers doigts de la main droite avec signe de Phalen et de Tinel positifs et début d''amyotrophie thénarienne.', 'حالة سريرية: موظفة مكتبية تبلغ 46 عاماً تشكو من خدر وتنميل ليلي في الإبهام والسبابة والوسطى مع إيجابية علامتي فالين وتينيل وضمور خفيف في الرانفة.', 0.5, 0.5),
('00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000041', 'physio-l6-vocab', 'physio', 6, 'choice', 'advanced', 'Physiologie', 'Cardiovasculaire', '{"kind":"choice","prompt":"What is the appropriate medical English diagnostic classification for this clinical presentation?","options":["Stage 2 Arterial Hypertension with left ventricular hypertrophy","Acute Myocardial Infarction","Orthostatic Hypotension","Cardiac Arrhythmia"],"correctAnswer":"Stage 2 Arterial Hypertension with left ventricular hypertrophy"}', 'What is the appropriate medical English diagnostic classification for this clinical presentation?', 'Quelle est la classification diagnostique médicale appropriée pour ce tableau clinique ?', 'ما هو التصنيف التشخيصي الطبي الأنسب لهذه الحالة السريرية؟', NULL, 'Stage 2 Arterial Hypertension with left ventricular hypertrophy', 35, 'Clinical Vignette: A 54-year-old asymptomatic executive presents for a routine executive health examination. Office blood pressure measurements across three separate visits average 168/102 mmHg bilaterally. Cardiovascular examination reveals an S4 atrial gallop rhythm. Fundoscopy demonstrates grade I arteriolar narrowing. The 12-lead ECG exhibits high voltage S waves in V1 and tall R waves in V5 (Sokolow-Lyon index >38 mm) with T-wave inversions consistent with left ventricular hypertrophy (LVH).', 'Vignette Clinique : Homme de 54 ans asymptomatique chez qui on découvre une PA moyenne de 168/102 mmHg avec galop B4 et des signes ECG évidents d''hypertrophie ventriculaire gauche.', 'حالة سريرية: رجل يبلغ 54 عاماً لا يشكو من أعراض ولديه قياسات متكررة لضغط الدم تبلغ 168/102 mmHg مع وجود صوت قلبي رابع وتضخم البطين الأيسر في التخطيط.', 0.5, 0.5),
('00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000042', 'anapath-l6-vocab', 'anapath', 6, 'choice', 'advanced', 'Anatomie Pathologique', 'Jonction Neuromusculaire', '{"kind":"choice","prompt":"Autoantibodies against which receptor are the primary cause of this patient''s fatigable weakness (Myasthenia Gravis)?","options":["Nicotinic acetylcholine receptors (AChR)","Voltage-gated calcium channels","Muscarinic acetylcholine receptors","Beta-1 adrenergic receptors"],"correctAnswer":"Nicotinic acetylcholine receptors (AChR)"}', 'Autoantibodies against which receptor are the primary cause of this patient''s fatigable weakness (Myasthenia Gravis)?', 'Des auto-anticorps dirigés contre quel récepteur sont la cause principale de cette faiblesse fluctuante (Myasthénie) ?', 'ضد أي مستقبلات تستهدف الأجسام المضادة الذاتية المسببة لهذا الضعف المتقلب (الوهن العضلي الوبيل)؟', NULL, 'Nicotinic acetylcholine receptors (AChR)', 35, 'Clinical Vignette: A 32-year-old female presents with fluctuating bilateral eyelid drooping (ptosis) and double vision (diplopia) that worsen notably in the evening or after reading. Over the past month, she has developed difficulty chewing tough meats and mild proximal arm weakness. Physical exam confirms fatigable ptosis during 60 seconds of sustained upward gaze. Deep tendon reflexes and sensation are normal. An ice pack applied over the closed eyes for 2 minutes produces immediate resolution of the ptosis.', 'Vignette Clinique : Femme de 32 ans présentant un ptosis et une diplopie fluctuants à prédominance vespérale. Le test du glaçon est positif, en faveur d''une myasthénie auto-immune.', 'حالة سريرية: شابة تبلغ 32 عاماً تعاني من تدلي الجفون وازدواج الرؤية الذي يزداد مساءً، مع إيجابية اختبار كيس الثلج المميز لمرض الوهن العضلي الوبيل.', 0.5, 0.5),
('00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000043', 'anapath-l6-vocab', 'anapath', 6, 'choice', 'advanced', 'Anatomie Pathologique', 'Urgences Abdominales', '{"kind":"choice","prompt":"What is the primary surgical clinical diagnosis for this acute abdomen?","options":["Acute Appendicitis","Nephrolithiasis","Acute Cholecystitis","Gastroenteritis"],"correctAnswer":"Acute Appendicitis"}', 'What is the primary surgical clinical diagnosis for this acute abdomen?', 'Quel est le diagnostic chirurgical principal devant ce tableau d''abdomen aigu ?', 'ما هو التشخيص الجراحي الأولي الأهم لهذه الحالة البطنية الإسعافية الحادة؟', NULL, 'Acute Appendicitis', 35, 'Clinical Vignette: A 19-year-old male student presents to the Emergency Department with acute abdominal pain of 14 hours'' duration. The pain started in the epigastric and periumbilical regions before migrating to the right lower quadrant (RLQ). He reports anorexia and low-grade nausea. Temperature is 38.3°C. Examination reveals exquisite localized tenderness at McBurney''s point with guarding, rebound tenderness, and a positive Rovsing sign.', 'Vignette Clinique : Étudiant de 19 ans présentant une douleur de la fosse iliaque droite migratrice depuis la région péri-ombilicale avec défense au point de McBurney et signe de Rovsing positif.', 'حالة سريرية: شاب يبلغ 19 عاماً يشكو من ألم بطني حاد بدأ حول السرة وانتقل للحفرة الحرقفية اليمنى مع حمى ودفاع بطني عند نقطة ماك بورني.', 0.5, 0.5),
('00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000044', 'anapath-l6-vocab', 'anapath', 6, 'choice', 'advanced', 'Anatomie Pathologique', 'Membre Supérieur', '{"kind":"choice","prompt":"What is the classic eponymic medical diagnosis for this distal radius fracture with dorsal displacement?","options":["Colles'' fracture","Smith''s fracture","Scaphoid fracture","Boxer''s fracture"],"correctAnswer":"Colles'' fracture"}', 'What is the classic eponymic medical diagnosis for this distal radius fracture with dorsal displacement?', 'Quel est le diagnostic éponymique classique pour cette fracture de l''extrémité inférieure du radius avec déplacement dorsal ?', 'ما هو التشخيص الاسمي الكلاسيكي لكسر أسفل عظم الكعبرة مع انزياح ظهري لقطعة الكسر؟', NULL, 'Colles'' fracture', 35, 'Clinical Vignette: A 68-year-old woman falls on her outstretched hand on a sidewalk. She presents with severe wrist pain and deformity. Inspection reveals the classic ''dinner-fork'' dorsal angulation deformity of the right distal forearm and wrist with edema and point tenderness over the distal radial metaphysis. Radial pulse is strong and neurovascular status of the hand is intact.', 'Vignette Clinique : Femme de 68 ans présentant une déformation en ''dos de fourchette'' du poignet droit après chute sur la main en extension, typique d''une fracture de Pouteau-Colles.', 'حالة سريرية: سيدة تبلغ 68 عاماً سقطت على يدها الممدودة وظهر لديها تشوه عظمي مميز يشبه شوكة الطعام في أسفل الساعد الأيمن متوافق مع كسر كولز.', 0.5, 0.5)
